Throwing an Error in the `proc.on('exit')` callback causes Node.js to crash with `TypeError: The "code" argument must be of type number. Received an instance of Error` when TypeScript compilation fails.

## Changes

- **Replace throw with reject**: Use `reject(new Error(...))` instead of `throw` in the exit callback to properly propagate errors through the promise chain
- **Add spawn error handler**: Add `proc.on('error')` to catch process spawn failures
- **Add watch mode error handling**: Add error handler to watch mode spawn to prevent uncaught exceptions

## Before
```javascript
tsBuildDone = Promise.resolve().then(async () => {
  await new Promise((resolve) => {
    const proc = spawn(tscPath, args, { stdio: 'inherit', shell: true });
    proc.on('exit', (code) => {
      if (code !== 0) {
        throw Error('TypeScript build failed');  // ← crashes Node.js
      }
      resolve();
    });
  });
  // ...
});
```

## After
```javascript
tsBuildDone = new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
  const proc = spawn(tscPath, args, { stdio: 'inherit', shell: true });
  proc.on('exit', (code) => {
    if (code !== 0) {
      reject(new Error('TypeScript build failed'));  // ← proper rejection
    } else {
      resolve();
    }
  });
  proc.on('error', (err) => reject(err));
}).then(async () => {
  // ...
});
```

