The `responseCheck` closure in `warnOnNoResponse` captured `iframeSettings` at timeout creation time, causing it to reference a stale object even after the iframe was removed from `settings[id]`.

## Changes

- Check `settings[id]` directly in `responseCheck` instead of captured variable
- Re-fetch `iframeSettings` from `settings[id]` after the closed check
- Add test case verifying warnings are suppressed for iframes removed during timeout period

**Before:**
```javascript
export default function warnOnNoResponse(id, settings) {
  function responseCheck() {
    if (hasClosed(iframeSettings)) return  // checks stale captured reference
    resetTimeout(iframeSettings)
    // ...
  }
  const iframeSettings = settings[id]
  iframeSettings.msgTimeout = setTimeout(responseCheck, warningTimeout)
}
```

**After:**
```javascript
export default function warnOnNoResponse(id, settings) {
  function responseCheck() {
    if (hasClosed(settings[id])) return  // checks current state
    const iframeSettings = settings[id]  // fetch after validation
    resetTimeout(iframeSettings)
    // ...
  }
  const iframeSettings = settings[id]
  iframeSettings.msgTimeout = setTimeout(responseCheck, warningTimeout)
}
```

